BT /F2 16 Tf 54 723 Td (TesseraCloud Administrator Guide) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 701 Td (Document ID: prod-tesseracloud-admin-guide | Version: 2025.2 | Effective: 2025-07-14 | Owner:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 688 Td (TesseraCloud Product Team, Meridian Instruments Ltd) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 663 Td (1. Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 641 Td (TesseraCloud is Meridian Instruments' software-as-a-service platform for the Tessera) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 628 Td (vibration-monitoring system. It receives telemetry from TS-4 gateways and their TS-4e edge) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 615 Td (nodes, stores readings, evaluates alarm policies and presents condition information to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 602 Td (maintenance and reliability teams. This guide is written for customer administrators, that is,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 589 Td (users holding the Tenant Owner or Site Admin role, and for Meridian partners who administer) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 576 Td (tenants on a customer's behalf.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 554 Td (This edition corresponds to the TesseraCloud 2025.2 release \(July 2025\). It introduces the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 541 Td (per-plan API rate limits described in the TesseraCloud API Rate Limits document) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 528 Td (\(prod-tesseracloud-api-rate-limits-v2\), the revised data retention settings in section 8, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 515 Td (the certificate re-provisioning procedure in section 11.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 493 Td (TesseraCloud is offered in two subscription plans, priced per monitored asset per year:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 471 Td (- Standard \(SKU TC-SUB-STD\): core monitoring, alarm policies, email and Microsoft Teams) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 458 Td (   notifications, 13 months of raw reading retention.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 445 Td (- Enterprise \(SKU TC-SUB-ENT\): everything in Standard plus SCIM user provisioning, SMS) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 432 Td (   notifications, 36 months of raw reading retention, higher API limits and the advanced) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 419 Td (   analytics workspace.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 403 Td (2. Tenancy and data residency) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 380 Td (2.1 Tenants) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 358 Td (Each customer organisation is provisioned as one tenant. A tenant is identified by a tenant ID) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 345 Td (in the format TC-T-NNNNNN \(for example TC-T-004817\), shown under Settings > Tenant > Overview.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 332 Td (All users, sites, gateways, nodes, alarm policies and API keys belong to exactly one tenant.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 319 Td (Data is never shared between tenants.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 297 Td (Large organisations sometimes ask for separate tenants per business unit. Meridian recommends a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 284 Td (single tenant with multiple sites instead, because cross-site reporting, shared alarm policies) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 271 Td (and single sign-on are all tenant-scoped.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 248 Td (2.2 Hosting regions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 226 Td (When a tenant is created, it is assigned to one hosting region, which cannot be changed later) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 213 Td (without a data migration project:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 192 Td (Region code | Hosting location | Typical customers) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 180 Td (EU1 | Amsterdam, Netherlands | UK, EU, Middle East) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 168 Td (US1 | Central United States | Americas) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 156 Td (AP1 | Singapore | Asia-Pacific, including Malaysia) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 134 Td (All readings, configuration and audit data for the tenant remain in its region. Backups are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 121 Td (replicated to a second availability zone within the same region.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 98 Td (2.3 Tenant Owner responsibilities) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 76 Td (Every tenant must have at least two users with the Tenant Owner role. TesseraCloud prevents) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 63 Td (removing or demoting the last remaining Tenant Owner. Tenant Owners receive service) Tj ET
endstream
endobj
