BT /F2 13 Tf 54 717 Td (5. Sites and assets) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 694 Td (5.1 Sites) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 672 Td (A site represents a physical location, such as a plant or a pumping station. Create sites at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 659 Td (Sites > Add Site. Each site has a name, a time zone, an address and an optional site code used) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 646 Td (in reports. Standard tenants can create up to 50 sites; Enterprise tenants have no site limit.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 624 Td (The site time zone controls how daily reports and business-hours notification rules are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 611 Td (evaluated. Readings are always stored in UTC.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 588 Td (5.2 Assets and measurement points) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 566 Td (An asset is a monitored machine, such as a pump, fan, motor or gearbox. Each asset contains one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 553 Td (or more measurement points, and each measurement point is bound to exactly one TS-4e edge node.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 540 Td (Assets are created at Sites > [site] > Assets > Add Asset.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 518 Td (For each asset, record:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 496 Td (- Machine type and machine class \(used for ISO 10816-3 alarm defaults; see the Tessera Alarm) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 483 Td (   Configuration Guide, prod-tessera-alarm-configuration-guide\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 470 Td (- Rated power and running speed.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 457 Td (- Foundation type \(rigid or flexible\).) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 444 Td (- Criticality \(A, B or C\), used to prioritise alarm routing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 431 Td (Asset subscriptions are counted per asset, not per node. An asset with four measurement points) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 418 Td (consumes one TC-SUB-STD or TC-SUB-ENT subscription.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 393 Td (6. Gateway fleet management) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 370 Td (6.1 Fleet view) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 348 Td (Fleet > Gateways lists all gateways in the tenant with their status \(Online, Offline,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 335 Td (Degraded\), firmware version, backhaul type, last heartbeat and number of paired nodes. A) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 322 Td (gateway is marked Offline after 10 minutes without a heartbeat. Degraded means the gateway is) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 309 Td (online but reporting at least one active T-code event.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 286 Td (6.2 Adding gateways) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 264 Td (Gateways are claimed using the serial number and claim code on the rating label \(Fleet >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 251 Td (Gateways > Add Gateway\). Full installation instructions are in the Tessera TS-4 Gateway) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 238 Td (Installation Guide \(prod-ts4-gateway-installation-guide\).) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 215 Td (6.3 Transferring a gateway to another site) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 193 Td (A gateway and all of its paired nodes can be moved from one site to another within the same) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 180 Td (tenant, for example when a skid is relocated. Go to Fleet > Gateways > [gateway] > Actions >) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 167 Td (Transfer Site, choose the destination site and confirm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 145 Td (Behaviour on transfer:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 123 Td (- The paired nodes move with the gateway. Their asset and measurement point bindings are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 110 Td (   cleared and must be re-created in the destination site.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 97 Td (- Historical readings remain associated with the original site and assets. They are not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 84 Td (   moved.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 71 Td (- Active alarms on the original assets are closed with the reason "Gateway transferred".) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 58 Td (- A transfer can only be performed by a user who is Site Admin on both sites, or a Tenant) Tj ET
endstream
