BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (   Owner.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (Transfers between tenants are not possible through the portal. A gateway must be released) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (\(Actions > Release Gateway\) by the current tenant and claimed by the new tenant using the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 690 Td (original claim code.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 667 Td (6.4 Firmware management) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 645 Td (Firmware updates are scheduled at Fleet > Gateways > [gateway] > Firmware > Schedule Update, or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 632 Td (in bulk from Fleet > Firmware Campaigns. A campaign can target up to 200 gateways and can be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 619 Td (limited to a maintenance window. TesseraCloud checks the firmware compatibility rules before) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 606 Td (scheduling: it will refuse to schedule node firmware 2.8.0 onto nodes whose gateway is not) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 593 Td (already on 5.3.0.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 571 Td (From 1 October 2025, TesseraCloud requires gateway firmware 5.2.0 or later. Gateways on 5.1.x) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 558 Td (will still connect after that date but will be shown as Degraded and cannot receive) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 545 Td (configuration changes until updated.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 520 Td (7. Alarm policies) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 497 Td (7.1 Policy structure) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 475 Td (An alarm policy defines when an alarm is raised and who is notified. A policy has:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 453 Td (- Scope: tenant-wide, site or individual asset.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 440 Td (- Conditions: metric \(velocity RMS, acceleration peak, crest factor, temperature, node) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 427 Td (   battery\), comparison and threshold.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 414 Td (- Persistence: the number of consecutive readings that must breach the threshold before the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 401 Td (   alarm is raised. The default is 3.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388 Td (- Severity: Warning or Alarm.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 375 Td (- Escalation plan: up to 3 escalation levels.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 362 Td (Asset-level policies override site-level policies, which override tenant-wide policies, for the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 349 Td (same metric.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 326 Td (7.2 Acknowledgement and escalation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 304 Td (When an alarm is raised, level 1 recipients are notified. If the alarm is not acknowledged) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 291 Td (within the acknowledgement timeout \(default 15 minutes, configurable from 5 to 240 minutes\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 278 Td (level 2 recipients are notified, and so on to level 3. Acknowledging an alarm stops escalation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 265 Td (but does not clear the alarm; an alarm clears automatically when readings fall below the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 252 Td (threshold minus the hysteresis band for the persistence count.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 54 229 Td (7.3 Suppression) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 207 Td (Alarm suppression rules can silence notifications during known events such as start-up) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 194 Td (transients. Suppression is set per asset at Sites > [site] > Assets > [asset] > Suppression.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 181 Td (Readings continue to be recorded during suppression.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 156 Td (8. Notification channels) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 134 Td (TesseraCloud supports the following channels:) Tj ET
BT /F2 9 Tf 54 113 Td (Channel | Plans | Notes) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 101 Td (Email | Standard, Enterprise | Sent from alerts@tesseracloud.meridian-instruments.com) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 89 Td (Microsoft Teams | Standard, Enterprise | Incoming webhook per channel) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 77 Td (Generic webhook | Standard, Enterprise | HTTPS POST, JSON payload, HMAC-SHA256 signature header) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 54 65 Td (X-Tessera-Signature) Tj ET
endstream
